-- The cross-IMPORT refusal (`export-refused.l4`, §11.19 OF-7) for an export whose
-- INPUT is a record with a field DEFAULT that reaches the imported reader. A
-- request that leaves the field out takes its default, so the export reaches an
-- imported reader exactly as a body that called it would, and the same three
-- things are true at once: the schema does not list `the rate`, a value sent under
-- that name is accepted and dropped, and discharge does not cross an IMPORT, so the
-- evaluation runs out as an internal error ("running bin op with invalid
-- operation") and not as an answer. It is refused at check time instead
-- (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md W7, §4.3, second review: the refusal for an
-- export's input default, `default-refused.l4`, had left this one open).

IMPORT `implicit-rate-lib`

DECLARE Config HAS
  markup IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (`scaled by the rate` 100)
  retries IS A NUMBER

@export What this amount comes to with a configured markup.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      cfg IS A Config
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cost with config` MEANS amount PLUS cfg's markup
